# REQUIRES: cuda
# The template in a reduced triclinic cell, a rhombic dodecahedron of 3,224
# TIP3P waters (Inputs/water_template_dodecahedron.py), PME, NPT with
# C-RESCALE, 2 fs, against the independent all-pairs, all-near-images check
# of every evaluated frame (MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE): no site pair
# within the cutoff without an inner entry, and no entry twice. At 1.5
# cutoffs, beyond every inner reach, the check must find pairs without one.
# The packing puts every reference point of a build in [0,1) on the lattice
# frame, so the members of no row group lie in two frames, and the search
# splits no row's entries by frame (the sequential Cartesian central image
# gave 15 % of the inner entries of this fixture as second entries of a
# row group for one partner unit).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/run %t/wide
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_dodecahedron.py %S/Inputs/triclinic %t/run 50 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CELL
# RUN: cd %t/run && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1 mdir run control.toml | tee run.log | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/water_template_dodecahedron.py %S/Inputs/triclinic %t/wide 10
# RUN: cd %t/wide && env MDIR_TEMPLATE_CHECK_COVERAGE=1.5 mdir run control.toml 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WIDE
# CELL: dodecahedron: 3224 waters, a = 5.20 nm, c_z = 3.6770 nm
# CHECK: template coverage checks {{[1-9][0-9]*}}: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} unit pairs within the cutoff, 0 without an entry, 0 duplicate entries; {{[1-9][0-9]*}} inner row groups, 0 in more than one lattice frame
# WIDE: template coverage checks {{[1-9][0-9]*}}: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} unit pairs within the cutoff, {{[1-9][0-9]*}} without an entry, 0 duplicate entries
